---
title: Soft Molasses Cookies
author: Aunt Lena Thorson
category: Cookies
cook time: 15 minutes
source: Loving Memories of Mildred
---

@flour{4%cups}
@baking soda{2%tsp}
@ginger{1.5%tsp}
@shortening, melted{1%cup}
@sugar{0.25%cup}
@salt{1.5%tsp}
@cinnamon{2%tsp}
@cloves{0.5%tsp}
@molasses{1.5%cups}
@egg{1}

Add molasses and sugar to melted shortening. Cool slightly. Stir in egg and gradually add flour with spices. Chill dough until stiff enough to handle. Make into 1 1/2 inch balls and place on greased cookie sheet about 2 inches apart. Bake for 15 minutes or until brown at 350 degrees. Makes about 5 dozen.
